   "text": {
    "L1": "At a war memorial, people stand silent to honour soldiers who gave their lives for us.",
    "L2": "Homage means special respect or honour. Sacrifice means giving something important for others.",
    "L3": "Grandpa served in the mountains for twenty years, and he is proud of his comrades.",
    "L4": "Now let us report his words: Grandpa said, “I am proud of my comrades.”",
    "L5": "In reported speech, I changes to he because Grandpa is speaking about himself.",
    "L6": "The tense also steps back: am becomes was. So we say, “Grandpa said that he was proud of his comrades.”",
    "L7": "Remembering soldiers is about service, teamwork, and sacrifice, not the excitement of fighting.",
    "L8": "Your turn: choose the correct report of Grandpa’s words."
   },
